1
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:16,110
Is that the last one?

2
00:00:16,110 --> 00:00:16,920
Yes.

3
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:26,540
I doubt Ketil's forces
have any will to fight left.

4
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:30,080
I'll send a messenger
recommending they surrender.

5
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:31,740
Your Majesty.

6
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,450
Would it be all right if we
requisitioned some homes on the farm?

7
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:42,000
My men are tired of camping out in tents.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:42,990
No.

9
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:47,360
All forces are forbidden
from entering the farm.

10
00:00:48,310 --> 00:00:51,020
If the soldiers enter the village,
they'll begin pillaging.

11
00:00:51,710 --> 00:00:54,930
Pillaging is the victor's right.

12
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:00,920
The goal of this battle is to requisition
the entire farm, not pillage it.

13
00:01:02,410 --> 00:01:07,420
I shall provide the Jomsvikings
with an adequate reward.

14
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:12,120
As you command.

15
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:28,960
You're showing them mercy now, Canute?

16
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:36,430
You are right. This is what a king does.

17
00:01:37,270 --> 00:01:39,710
To achieve his grand purpose,

18
00:01:39,710 --> 00:01:45,530
he spares those who should live,
and slays those he must kill.

19
00:01:45,910 --> 00:01:49,240
The masses could never bear
such a heavy responsibility.

20
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:55,620
This world is still far from
being a paradise. It's hell.

21
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:59,670
And hell has its own laws.

22
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:08,160
Canute, you killed your
father and your brother.

23
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:15,230
Keep killing until your
corpse-lined road reaches paradise.

24
00:02:54,150 --> 00:03:00,670
Thank you, Einar and Thorfinn.

25
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,690
Thank you.

26
00:05:13,070 --> 00:05:17,780
Courage.

27
00:05:37,630 --> 00:05:39,220
Hold him still.

28
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:41,060
It's no use. He's already dead.

29
00:05:41,060 --> 00:05:42,930
I need hot water over here.

30
00:05:42,930 --> 00:05:45,080
Kill me!

31
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:47,370
Young master...

32
00:05:51,610 --> 00:05:52,960
Young master...

33
00:05:56,940 --> 00:06:01,870
My father's hands are gone.

34
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:19,200
Y-Y-Young master, please look
after my daughter and family.

35
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:36,690
You can't even cut a pig.

36
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:45,950
Young master?

37
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:54,960
Young master!

38
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:03,480
Are you all right?

39
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:06,470
Are you injured as well?

40
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:12,300
Is it your stomach? Does your stomach hurt?

41
00:07:13,960 --> 00:07:15,870
You should lie down.

42
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:33,290
They have advised us to
surrender a second time.

43
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:38,040
The entire clan surrendering is
their condition for a truce.

44
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:41,710
You'll still be subjected to outlawry.

45
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:48,000
You need to decide if we'll
continue fighting or surrender.

46
00:07:48,390 --> 00:07:50,850
Y-You can't be serious!

47
00:07:51,170 --> 00:07:54,670
I refuse to be banished from the country.

48
00:07:54,670 --> 00:07:58,110
What do they expect us to do?
Leave this land and become beggars?

49
00:07:58,110 --> 00:08:02,540
Snake, this happened because
you're a spineless coward.

50
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:06,190
You freeloader!

51
00:08:08,620 --> 00:08:09,760
Boss!

52
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:11,200
You hag!

53
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:12,520
Don't, Fox.

54
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:18,500
If we say we'll keep fighting,
what will you do, Snake?

55
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:22,260
Fight along with you.

56
00:08:25,110 --> 00:08:26,890
That's what I wanted to hear.

57
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:30,910
Don't worry, Mom. I'll handle this.

58
00:08:30,910 --> 00:08:35,770
Twenty men is enough
to take the king's head.

59
00:08:38,150 --> 00:08:43,100
Defeating a larger force with only a handful
of men is a glorious way for a man to go out.

60
00:08:44,150 --> 00:08:46,750
Calm down, Thorgil.

61
00:08:46,750 --> 00:08:49,740
That's not your decision to make.

62
00:08:50,130 --> 00:08:53,040
What? No, it's gotta be me.

63
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:55,520
Dad's out of it.

64
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:58,170
Are you saying you want to decide, Grandpa?

65
00:08:58,670 --> 00:09:00,590
It's not my decision, either.

66
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:06,570
There's someone Ketil
named as his successor.

67
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:35,450
We'll surrender.

68
00:09:36,150 --> 00:09:37,040
What?

69
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:39,300
How could you say that?

70
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:42,290
Doesn't that embarrass you as a Norse man?

71
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:49,870
It's embarrassing.

72
00:09:50,950 --> 00:09:52,430
It's embarrassing, but...

73
00:09:54,330 --> 00:09:55,550
I'm scared.

74
00:09:56,810 --> 00:10:01,780
I'm scared of people dying.

75
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:03,960
I'm scared I might die.

76
00:10:05,450 --> 00:10:07,760
They can banish me or do
whatever else they want with me.

77
00:10:08,370 --> 00:10:12,450
I just want this to be over.

78
00:10:14,330 --> 00:10:16,580
You can't be serious, Olmar.

79
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:19,700
You wanted so badly to fight.

80
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:23,080
You're the one who started this war.

81
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:26,910
That's right. It's my fault.

82
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:30,590
They mocked me for screwing up.

83
00:10:31,190 --> 00:10:33,160
I got mad and tried to show off.

84
00:10:35,350 --> 00:10:37,980
I'm sorry to Mom and everyone else.

85
00:10:38,730 --> 00:10:44,240
But because I started this,
I want to end this.

86
00:10:47,570 --> 00:10:51,560
Sorry, I misspoke.

87
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:55,990
The king wanted this farm from the start.

88
00:10:56,740 --> 00:11:00,750
But I gave them an excuse to start a war.

89
00:11:01,810 --> 00:11:06,510
People will always find a reason to fight.

90
00:11:06,510 --> 00:11:09,460
If it wasn't you, it
would've been me or Dad.

91
00:11:10,060 --> 00:11:12,810
You defended your honor then.

92
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:16,240
Right, Olmar? You did good.

93
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:18,470
Your honor is more
important than your life.

94
00:11:19,290 --> 00:11:23,370
Show us the courage of a
Norse warrior one more time.

95
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:26,110
No!

96
00:11:29,610 --> 00:11:32,990
That's not courage!

97
00:11:33,980 --> 00:11:37,870
I screwed up in the presence of the king.

98
00:11:38,810 --> 00:11:42,460
I'm an incompetent man
who deserves to be mocked.

99
00:11:42,900 --> 00:11:44,140
But...

100
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:48,540
But...

101
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:58,160
I didn't have the courage to
silently accept their mockery.

102
00:12:06,050 --> 00:12:10,520
I can't be like you, Brother.

103
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:14,300
I don't care about
the honor of Norse warriors.

104
00:12:16,790 --> 00:12:18,440
I'm going to surrender.

105
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:21,260
Mock me if you want.

106
00:12:33,770 --> 00:12:37,430
The acting head of the family
has made his decision.

107
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:42,520
Olmar, go tell King Canute your decision.

108
00:12:47,980 --> 00:12:49,530
I'll go with you.

109
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:59,230
I won't mock you, young master.

110
00:13:04,630 --> 00:13:06,290
I don't have time for this crap.

111
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:10,170
Move. You're in the way.

112
00:13:11,530 --> 00:13:14,170
Wait. Where are you going, Thorgil?

113
00:13:14,430 --> 00:13:15,640
Shut up.

114
00:13:16,250 --> 00:13:18,480
Later, cowards.

115
00:13:32,790 --> 00:13:39,150
It's true that many have been
supported by your strength.

116
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:44,650
But I know you've seen it, too.

117
00:13:45,830 --> 00:13:51,390
How those possessed by
wealth and power end up.

118
00:13:56,330 --> 00:14:00,570
But you haven't lost
all of this for nothing.

119
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:09,900
In exchange for your farm,
your son has become a man.

120
00:14:20,410 --> 00:14:21,610
Why?

121
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:24,120
Why did you let him go?

122
00:14:24,630 --> 00:14:29,000
Haven't you been looking for
Thorfinn all this time?

123
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:33,690
Didn't you come here to
take Thorfinn back home?

124
00:14:35,930 --> 00:14:42,510
You're right. That oath has
kept me going all this time.

125
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:48,400
No matter how many times I lost him,
I kept looking for him.

126
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:53,440
I won't break my oath to my friend.

127
00:14:54,840 --> 00:15:00,400
But Thorfinn is being moved by
something bigger than that now.

128
00:15:01,430 --> 00:15:04,880
Thorfinn said he'd come back.

129
00:15:06,220 --> 00:15:09,390
I trust what I saw in those eyes.

130
00:15:13,740 --> 00:15:14,640
Thorfinn...

131
00:15:40,590 --> 00:15:46,200
So, what? You're not part of
Ketil's clan, shorty?

132
00:15:47,430 --> 00:15:50,640
My name is Thorfinn, son of Thors.

133
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:53,710
I'm a retainer on this farm.

134
00:15:54,580 --> 00:15:57,290
I've come representing Ketil,
the owner of the farm.

135
00:15:57,980 --> 00:15:59,960
Please inform His Majesty
that I'm here to see him.

136
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:03,720
A retainer? You're a slave, aren't you?

137
00:16:06,490 --> 00:16:08,780
You can always tell when someone's a slave.

138
00:16:09,450 --> 00:16:11,980
They stink like livestock.

139
00:16:17,570 --> 00:16:21,120
You're not good enough.

140
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:25,740
We'll just keep fighting until
someone from Ketil's clan shows up.

141
00:16:27,450 --> 00:16:30,750
I've met His Majesty before.

142
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:34,190
He should know who I am
if you tell him my name.

143
00:16:34,190 --> 00:16:38,210
Please let him know Thorfinn,
son of Thors, is here.

144
00:16:45,690 --> 00:16:49,740
You and King Canute know each other?

145
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:57,050
About four years ago,
I served as his guard for a short while.

146
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:12,240
Did that wake you up, shorty?

147
00:17:13,020 --> 00:17:16,970
I've never seen a guard
as stinky and small as you.

148
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:21,200
If I offended you, then I apologize.

149
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:22,830
But it's true.

150
00:17:23,290 --> 00:17:25,390
Please tell His Majesty my name.

151
00:17:26,510 --> 00:17:28,140
Please.

152
00:17:28,140 --> 00:17:30,430
What's the matter, Drott?

153
00:17:30,430 --> 00:17:32,960
He's still talking nonsense.

154
00:17:32,960 --> 00:17:35,970
Apparently your punch was too weak.

155
00:17:37,950 --> 00:17:39,950
You don't wake easily.

156
00:17:39,950 --> 00:17:45,900
You must want me to get you up
gently like your mommy did, huh?

157
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:48,880
Get him!

158
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:50,530
You've got this, shorty!

159
00:17:50,530 --> 00:17:51,800
Come on!

160
00:17:54,700 --> 00:17:56,640
Did you determine
what the commotion is about?

161
00:17:57,120 --> 00:18:00,920
Yes, Your Majesty. Ketil sent a messenger.

162
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:06,580
Since Ketil himself hasn't come to surrender,
my men are attempting to send him away,

163
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:09,680
but he seems to be rather stubborn.

164
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:12,960
Did you get his name and status?

165
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:13,740
Yes, Your Majesty.

166
00:18:14,830 --> 00:18:19,940
He identified himself as a retainer on
the farm named Thorfinn, son of Thors.

167
00:18:27,050 --> 00:18:30,300
Is he a young and small man?

168
00:18:31,030 --> 00:18:33,040
Yes, indeed.

169
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:35,950
Do you know him?

170
00:18:39,460 --> 00:18:41,120
Get him!

171
00:18:43,980 --> 00:18:47,770
What would you like to do,
Your Majesty? Will you see him?

172
00:18:51,430 --> 00:18:54,100
No, that won't be necessary.

173
00:18:59,350 --> 00:19:01,470
Son of Thors...

174
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:03,770
Yeah, right.

175
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:05,520
Kill him!

176
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:06,820
Hit him back, shorty!

177
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:08,860
The eyes! Go for the eyes!

178
00:19:10,860 --> 00:19:13,320
Wait. I don't want to fight.

179
00:19:16,870 --> 00:19:19,620
Oh? He's got some moves.

180
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:25,120
What's the matter, Drott?

181
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:27,360
You haven't hit him yet.

182
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:27,710
Get your shit together!

183
00:19:29,950 --> 00:19:32,460
Damn. I underestimated them.

184
00:19:32,460 --> 00:19:35,120
In any case, I need
to change the situation.

185
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:39,090
Hit him already, Drott.

186
00:19:39,090 --> 00:19:41,520
We can't settle our wagers like this.

187
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:48,060
All right!

188
00:19:48,060 --> 00:19:50,150
That's the first one!

189
00:19:50,150 --> 00:19:52,160
Get him!

190
00:19:51,130 --> 00:19:53,150
He's still looking lively!

191
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:54,850
Kill him!

192
00:19:54,850 --> 00:19:55,730
Damn it.

193
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:58,120
Thorfinn!

194
00:19:58,540 --> 00:19:59,500
Are you all right?

195
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:02,460
Einar, what are you doing here?

196
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:06,000
You idiot. I came here to
stop you, obviously.

197
00:20:07,750 --> 00:20:08,720
Sorry.

198
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:15,230
Just get up. We're getting out of here.

199
00:20:15,230 --> 00:20:18,420
There's no point in talking to these guys.

200
00:20:18,420 --> 00:20:20,850
Come on, pay up.

201
00:20:23,050 --> 00:20:23,850
Thank you.

202
00:20:27,370 --> 00:20:28,610
Thorfinn?

203
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:31,610
What are you betting on?

204
00:20:33,940 --> 00:20:38,430
We're betting on how many punches
it'll take for you to run away crying.

205
00:20:38,430 --> 00:20:41,120
Including unconsciousness or death.

206
00:20:41,670 --> 00:20:44,450
The most popular bet is fewer than ten.

207
00:20:44,450 --> 00:20:47,600
A few have bet on more than 20.

208
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:50,460
Come on, you've got this.

209
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:52,880
One more hit, and you can go to sleep.

210
00:20:51,670 --> 00:20:53,260
Hang in there until you've taken ten.

211
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:55,960
They're unbelievable.

212
00:20:57,750 --> 00:21:01,390
I'd like in on that bet, too.

213
00:21:01,890 --> 00:21:04,270
I'll bet on myself.

214
00:21:06,820 --> 00:21:11,020
I don't need money if I win. Instead...

215
00:21:12,740 --> 00:21:15,600
I'd just like to talk to His Majesty.

216
00:21:20,500 --> 00:21:22,370
Did you guys hear that?

217
00:21:22,370 --> 00:21:25,160
Shorty just proposed
something real interesting.

218
00:21:26,230 --> 00:21:29,620
All right, fine. I like your guts.

219
00:21:29,620 --> 00:21:33,980
But we're not letting you get away
with betting on fewer than ten.

220
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:38,050
What has no one bet on yet?

221
00:21:38,050 --> 00:21:43,180
Well, at least one person's bet on
everything up to the nineties.

222
00:21:44,330 --> 00:21:46,860
100, then.

223
00:21:46,860 --> 00:21:50,060
If you can withstand 100 blows, you win.

224
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:54,070
If you lose, we'll take your life.

225
00:21:55,180 --> 00:21:56,240
Fine.

226
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:58,030
What? You...

227
00:21:59,130 --> 00:22:00,030
Thorfinn!

228
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:05,290
Do you have to risk that much for Ketil?

229
00:22:05,820 --> 00:22:08,260
This is war.

230
00:22:08,260 --> 00:22:10,820
There's nothing one man can do about it.

231
00:22:10,820 --> 00:22:14,920
Leave this fight to the ones who want it.

232
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:24,920
I'm glad I ended up on this farm.

233
00:22:26,580 --> 00:22:34,820
I only knew war, but the master,
Pater, and the old master...

234
00:22:35,840 --> 00:22:39,150
They didn't forsake me.
They were kind to me.

235
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:42,640
I got to meet you, too.

236
00:22:46,250 --> 00:22:49,660
You understand that, don't you?

237
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:55,640
Are you okay with not returning
the kindness we received?

238
00:23:02,460 --> 00:23:03,580
Thorfinn...

239
00:23:03,580 --> 00:23:05,220
It's all right, Einar.

240
00:23:07,050 --> 00:23:09,240
There's a trick to getting hit.

241
00:23:10,060 --> 00:23:12,720
And I'm used to getting hit.

242
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:15,300
Seriously?

243
00:23:15,300 --> 00:23:16,960
That's it, shorty!

244
00:23:16,960 --> 00:23:19,440
Get that big idiot!

245
00:23:21,560 --> 00:23:23,610
He thinks you're a wimp, Drott!

246
00:23:24,170 --> 00:23:26,280
Is your size just for show?

247
00:23:26,710 --> 00:23:29,130
Beat him already!

248
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:37,130
The great Drott the Bear Killer has
never been mocked like this before.

249
00:23:39,030 --> 00:23:40,860
I'll kill you.

250
00:23:42,010 --> 00:23:44,660
Is he stupid? He's gonna die!

251
00:23:44,660 --> 00:23:47,150
Make him last at least 20 hits!

252
00:23:47,150 --> 00:23:48,810
Kill him!

253
00:25:35,870 --> 00:25:40,080
The King of Rebellion.

254
00:25:37,210 --> 00:25:39,310
"The King of Rebellion."
